For the marker round-trip test, the RED expectation: currently the payload contains raw `-->` → body contains TWO occurrences of ` -->`... wait: `"not a defect: A --> B is handled upstream"` — contains ` -->` once (space before -->). Plus the marker suffix ` -->` = 2 occurrences of ' -->'. After the fix: only 1 (the real suffix).

Test details:
```js
suite('marker-safe payload — a --> in reviewer text cannot corrupt the registry marker', function() {

   function regWithOne(r) { ... } // same as existing helper but local

   test('a withdrawReason containing --> still round-trips through the marker', function() {
       var r = loadRegistry();
       var policy = r.resolveIdentityPolicy({}, null);
       var reg1 = r.applyRound(r.emptyRegistry(), { at: '2026-11-03T10:00:00Z',
           findings: [finding('src/auth.ts', 'nothing validates a token', 'BLOCKING', 45)] }, policy).registry;
       var out = r.applyRound(reg1, { at: '2026-11-03T11:00:00Z', findings: [],
           dispositions: [{ n: 1, status: 'withdrawn', reason: 'not a defect: A --> B is handled upstream' }] }, policy);
       var body = r.buildRegistryComment(out.registry);
       assert.ok(body.indexOf('<!-- dmtools:finding-registry ') === 0, 'the marker opens the comment');
       assert.equal(body.split(' -->').length - 1, 1, 'exactly one marker suffix — the injected --> was sanitized');
       var parsed = r.latestRegistry([machineComment(body)]);
       assert.ok(parsed, 'the round-2 registry still parses (state cannot silently revert)');
       assert.equal(parsed.registry.items[0].status, 'withdrawn');
       assert.ok(parsed.registry.items[0].withdrawReason.indexOf('A') !== -1, 'the reason text survives for display');
       assert.ok(parsed.registry.items[0].withdrawReason.indexOf('-->') === -1, 'no raw --> inside the payload');
   });
``

Wait — after sanitization, withdrawReason in the PAYLOAD becomes `not a defect: A --\u200b> B is handled upstream`. The parsed reason contains `--\u200b>` — so `indexOf('-->')` === -1 ✓ and indexOf('A') !== -1 ✓.

But hold on: does the REASON also need to survive in the IN-MEMORY registry (out.registry.items[0].withdrawReason === raw)? My fix sanitizes only at serialization → yes, in-memory keeps raw. I'll assert that too: `out.registry.items[0].withdrawReason` — raw preserved in memory. Hmm, but is that over-constraining? The reviewer suggested sanitizing "either in applyDisposition or in buildRegistryComment" — sanitizing at applyDisposition would store sanitized in memory. My choice: buildRegistryComment (the payload boundary) + escalation display. Keep the test focused on the contract: the marker must parse back; the display text must be preserved (modulo the zero-width joiner). I'll assert in-memory raw too since that's my design — it's the reviewer's "sanitized text preserved for display".

Hmm wait — actually, let me reconsider: display side (escalation packet) reads from the PARSED registry (loaded from the payload) in smAgent.js:6443. So the display text is the sanitized `--\u200b>` variant. And buildEscalationPacketComment ALSO gets used on... in smAgent it parses from comments → sanitized. If someone calls buildEscalationPacket on an in-memory registry (raw `-->`), the visible census line would contain `-->` — inside a VISIBLE comment body (not inside an HTML comment) that's harmless for parsing but the reviewer asked to treat it "so the visible census well-formed". I'll apply markerSafe to the rendered reason in buildEscalationPacketComment. Then even in-memory raw text renders sanitized. 

