arguments.content:
## Fixed — one shared helper, error policy kept at the call sites

Hoisted the ladder into `normalizePrCommentList(raw)` in `js/common/findingRegistry.js` (exported) — the leaf both wiring files already require:

```js
function normalizePrCommentList(raw) {
    var obj = (typeof raw === 'string') ? JSON.parse(raw) : (raw || []);
    return Array.isArray(obj) ? obj : (obj.comments || obj.items || []);
}
```

- `prCommentsForRegistry` (`js/postPRReviewComments.js`) delegates to it and keeps its **catch-and-null** policy (fail-closed: no comment list → no stamp).
- `prCommentListForRegistry` (`js/preparePRForReview.js`) delegates to it with **no local try/catch**, so a broken payload throws into `writeFindingRegistryContext`'s existing non-fatal catch — the per-site error policy from the suggestion is preserved verbatim.

Unit tests for the helper live in `test_findingRegistry.js` (suite "normalizePrCommentList — the one comment-shape ladder behind both wiring sites"): JSON-string input, already-parsed array, `{comments}` / `{items}` envelopes, shapeless object / null / undefined → `[]`, and a broken JSON string **throws** (policy stays at the call site).

As suggested, this also removed the three over-threshold CRAP functions in `postPRReviewComments.js` (`prCommentsForRegistry`, `stampFindingRegistry`, `postFindingRegistryUpdate` are now 5.0 / 7.0 / 7.8). Bonus: the duplication gate's over-threshold set shrank — `preparePRForReview.js` (1.10% duplicated lines on the previous head) leaves it entirely.

